[(Sometimes the \223padding\224 sticks to the piece after a pro\037)260( )49(le is cut. The vaporized acr)-40(ylic can condense as a liquid )]TJ
0 -1.2 TD
[(and solidify between the piece and the padding. The edge of a razor blad\e or knife can pr)-40(y the two apar)-20(t. )]TJ
0 -1.958 TD
[(Keep in mind that the laser beam has a \037)260( )49(nite width. In my case, around 0.2 mm. This means that if a laser cuts )]TJ
0 -1.2 TD
(along a rectangle 9 mm wide and 30 mm tall, it yields a block that is 8.\8 mm wide and 29.8 mm tall, and a )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
[(hole that is 9.2 mm wide and 30.2 mm tall. Since the par)-20(t is slightly smaller than the hole, it can wobble around )]TJ
0 -1.2 TD
[(and become misaligned when cutting the second pro\037)260( )48(le )]TJ
/T1_2 1 Tf
(\(pawn, step 5\))Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
[(. T)100(o \037)260( )49(x this, you could cut a seperate )]TJ
0 -1.2 TD
[(slightly smaller hole to \037)260( )49(t the piece more snugly)80(.)]TJ
0 -1.958 TD
(The laser beam cross-section is guassian\227it is most intense in the ce\nter and drops off as it moves radially out-)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(ward. As a result egdes cut by the beam have a slight angle. This can ma\ke the pieces stand not quite upright.)Tj
-0.003 Tc -0.001 Tw 0 -1.958 TD
[(What if you made V)60(-blocks that held the piece at 45\260 angles in the hole? Could you make\ an 8-sided chess piece?)]TJ
